<title>UK: BSkyB rises to new record on short squeeze.</title>
<headline>BSkyB rises to new record on short squeeze.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in BSkyB climbed to another record peak on Monday on what traders characterized as a short squeeze.</p>
<p>By 0858 GMT, the shares were up 9p to 659p, after rising as high as 661p earlier. They have jumped by about 15 percent during the last three weeks, with the rise accelerating after the shares broke through 600p.</p>
<p>&quot;I think the market is just short of stock,&quot; said one market maker of the recent advance in the shares.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
